# gap-afetch.sh - r23 (written 2026-11-09 at the desk, NOT RUN; only --dry-run and the --mock test ran; review fixes 11-09
# evening, the owner's rule answers set as the frozen switches): THE ADAPT_FETCH GAP (results/BACKLOG-1027.md section I;
# Karl 11-09: "queue its gap only after the v0.2.13 shape gap"; the design and the estimate
# results/r23/ADAPTFETCH-DESK-1109.md). P = P028x as served for tests (configs/P028x.json without the picture reader = x28h +
# STRATA_HC_UPMIX=1) on engine-r22p028x against F1 / F2 = the same config on engine-r23afetch (153ce47d3ef0, r23-adaptfetch)
# + STRATA_ADAPT_FETCH=1 / =2, the helper GPU on, as served. MEASUREMENTS ONLY: P028x stays served, nothing switches,
# nothing is built, no config of the served setup changes. The rules, fixed before any run and frozen into the gap's
# rules.txt: work/r23/afetch-gap/afetch_rules.py's docstring and its switches (B3_PROMPT_FORM, GAIN_FORM, ORDER_FORM). Started
# by afetch-after-shape.sh (a user unit) as a snapshot copy; every path here is absolute. Usage: gap-afetch.sh [--dry-run |
# --mock]; any other argument: nothing runs (exit 2). One instance at a time (tmp/afetch-gap.driver.pid: a second one exits
# 9 before it touches anything).
#   0 BEFORE THE GAP (no GPU; 8080 untouched). It REFUSES (nothing changed) - exit 1 = busy (the starter retries), exit 6 =
#     a hard refusal (an alert), exit 8 = HELD by the priority rule (final, an alert) - unless:
#     - the v0.2.13 shape gap has run (results/r23/port-0213/shape-gap/result.txt starts "DONE"; a kernel error, a failed
#       end, an interruption or a refusal keep this gap waiting: Karl looks at those first) and its unit shape-gap0213 is
#       inactive, else busy; the research queue is not held by anyone else (bench2.hold not this gap's), else busy;
#     - THE PRIORITY RULE (Karl 11-09): the Qwen4 watch (work/qwen4-kit/hfwatch/state.json) has no open Flash repo with
#       weights - a find HOLDS the gap (exit 8) unless tmp/afetch-priority-done has a dated reason line (the override,
#       written only when Karl says the day-one work is done: named in the summary, the decision and the result); a
#       missing or unreadable state file = busy (the rule cannot be checked);
#     - no other gap, no held test lock, no model server but 8080's P028x, nothing on 8081; nvidia-smi answers within 20 s;
#       the post-Phase-5 chain is not running; the kernel-log watcher runs and a kernel check passes;
#     - the files are there (the rules and tools, the stored exact7 x28h-e7a (7 items), gap 16's long40 (40 logit files),
#       gap 17's cold-M, the Basalt fixtures, the sampled harness and its spec); engine-r22p028x is f4c4f654fb24 with
#       STRATA_HC_UPMIX and port_gap4.sh restores that sha; engine-r23afetch is 153ce47d3ef0 with STRATA_ADAPT_FETCH and
#       _VERIFY and its SOURCE names r23-adaptfetch; >= 5 GB free;
#     - afetch_rules.py's selftest, copycheck and forms pass; the sampled harness's sq.py selftest (SELFTEST OK),
#       sq_client.py selftest (CLIENT SELFTEST OK) and sq.py selftest-real (SELFTEST-REAL OK) pass; `sq.py derive` of the
#       run's spec copy passes and `sq.py rule` writes sampled/rule.txt (BEFORE any engine starts); the arm configs check
#       out (afetch_rules.py arms + cfgcheck); the rules and the switches are frozen into rules.txt.
#   1 port_gap4.sh begin (the research queue held after its running question, the test lock, 8080 down; it waits for a Jan
#     job, a chat being answered, a DeepSeek session and a quiet window; GAP_MAX_MIN = the worst case below); the engines
#     gone and MemAvailable >= 40 GB (120 s at most; engines still there: the gap ends, exit 5 - they are named, never
#     killed); PRE = the engine processes running as the gap opened (8080's, stopping: P has the served P028x's binary):
#     no cleanup ever stops one of them, nor any engine started before the gap opened; a kernel check; the watchdog (one
#     critical alert if the gap is still open 20 min past the deadline); the priority rule again
#   2 BUILD VS SWITCH: exact7 F0 (P on engine-r23afetch, switch unset) at pin 2500 vs x28h-e7a; pf_yardstick long40 F0 vs
#     gap 16's x28h long40 (gap-basalt-speed.sh's e7 / pfy40, br e7gate / br same); afetch_rules.py exact -> build_switch.
#     Not PASS -> nothing below runs (the decision says so).
#   3 (ORDER_FORM vf-first, the owner's 11-09 order) THE READ-BACK START: VF (X2 + STRATA_ADAPT_FETCH_VERIFY=1 +
#     STRATA_ADAPT_CHECKRES=1, K 2, budget 300 s), sq.py verify, its verdict read from verify-VF.json. A mismatch: speed and
#     the sampled part do not run for either candidate (the decision says why; sq.py decide still writes its decision).
#     Neither PASS nor FAIL (not started, voided, a foreign GPU user, a crash): tried once more at the sampled part.
#   4 SPEED: B2 Basalt's decode fixtures (conv, struct, prose), a fresh engine per start, 3 passes; then B3 the 9-workload
#     screen (abarm.sh), a fresh engine per arm-pass, 3 passes; both in a Latin square (P F1 F2 / F2 P F1 / F1 F2 P). A
#     speed step starts only if it leaves the rest of the sampled part its minimum before the deadline.
#   5 QUALITY, the sampled-distribution test (work/r23/sampled-qwen/STEPS-adaptfetch.txt): VF first if it has not run
#     (ORDER_FORM speed-first); R1 (= P, K 8), X1 (= F1, K 8), X2 (= F2, K 8), R2 (= P again, K 4); with R1's samples: sq.py
#     ids and the scorer (guard.py + sq.py score --max-min 25 cut to the minutes left, sq.py envwatch --kill, a watchdog);
#     sq.py decide. The part starts only if its minimum fits; each served arm only if it and the rest fit.
#   6 afetch_rules.py decide -> decision.txt / .json; the lock sweep (nothing of this gap may still run or hold the test
#     lock); port_gap4.sh end (P028x back); a kernel check; result.txt, a NOTES.md line, a non-urgent ntfy note. NOTHING
#     SWITCHES: Karl decides.
# The priority rule is checked again before each long part (each exactness run, the read-back start, each speed pass, the
# sampled part and each of its arms): a find stops new steps, the decision is written on what ran and the gap ends cleanly
# (P028x back): exit 8 and an alert.
# Every test server: no foreign GPU user before it (60 s) or during it (a 5 s watch: the start is left out; nvidia-smi not
# answering within 20 s counts as not clear); its engine's env checked before it measures (basalt_rules envcheck +
# afetch_rules fetchenv; the sampled arms: + sq.py envcheck); the start line (afetch_rules startline); the fatal-line check;
# after it, however it ended, test_cleanup (the guard, server.py, the 8081 server, the monitor, this gap's engines): if
# anything had to be stopped the start is VOIDED (left out); a kernel check. CLI jobs (exact7, pf_yardstick, the scorer):
# their engines checked as they start by /proc/PID/exe (br envcli / sq.py envwatch --kill). Children run with 8>&- 9>&- and
# stdin from /dev/null; processes are found by PID, pid file or exact name (pgrep -x) only.
# TIME with 8080 down (the Basalt speed gap's measured step times of 11-09 and STEPS-adaptfetch.txt's plan): open ~2,
# exact7 ~3.5 + long40 ~9 = ~12, VF ~5, B2 9 starts x ~1.65 = ~15, B3 9 arm-passes x ~3.7 = ~33, the rest of the sampled
# part ~30 (R1/X1/X2 11, R2 2.2, ids 0.5, scorer ~16, decide 0.5), decide + close ~4 -> ~100 min (~1.7 h; ~1.5-2.0 h).
# Deadline AF_MAX_MIN (default 150) minutes after the gap opens for any new step; a step starts only if its minimum fits
# (exact7 5, long40 10, VF 7, a B2 start 3, a screen arm-pass 5, the rest of the sampled part 38: R1/X1/X2 5 each, R2 3, ids
# 1, scorer 18, decide 1). WORST CASE ~2.9 h with 8080 down (175 min = GAP_MAX_MIN): the deadline 150 + the longest
# overrun of a step started inside its minimum (~7: a K8 sampled arm's 600-s request budget + its start / stop against its
# 5-min minimum; the scorer's --max-min is cut to the time left) + the decisions ~2 + the lock sweep and port_gap4.sh end
# (<= 120 s engines + <= 180 s memory + the restart) ~8 + the open's engine wait ~2 = ~169, rounded up. The test lock goes
# about 3 min before the restart ends, so the watchdog (open 20 min past the deadline) fires only on a real hang.
# THE KERNEL-ERROR POLICY (Karl 11-09; the shape gap's form): any new Xid or kernel error (kwatch's tmp/r19/KERNEL_ERROR,
# polled every 5 s inside every GPU watch: this gap's programs are killed at once, $O/kerr.seen; checked before every
# step; or a kernel check failing) stops the gap at once: the lock sweep, port_gap4.sh end (P028x back), a critical alert
# ("stopped at once, P028x back" or "8080 NOT back"), the result "KERNEL ERROR during the gap - stopped at once, ...",
# exit 3. kwatch is NOT cleared.
# Exit 0 done (the outcome is in decision.txt), 1 busy (refused, nothing changed), 2 a bad argument (nothing run), 3 a
# kernel error / kernel check failure (stopped at once; P028x back unless the result says "8080 NOT back"), 4 port_gap4.sh
# end failed, 5 not run: engines still running after 8080 stopped (P028x back;
# the starter alerts), 6 hard refusal (alert), 7 stopped by a signal (alert), 8 the priority rule (held before the gap, or
# the gap ended early; alert), 9 another instance runs (nothing touched).
# --dry-run: the pre-gap checks (a refusal is printed and the plan goes on), afetch_rules.py's selftest / arms / priority /
# shapecheck / forms, and the plan of every command, printed; no lock, no GPU query, no kernel check, no sampled-harness
# command, no port_gap4; writes only under work/r23/afetch-gap/scratch/.
# --mock: (work/r23/afetch-gap/gap-mock-test.sh only) every tool a stub under work/r23/afetch-gap/scratch/mock; the rules
# script runs for real on the stubs' synthetic data; never kills a real process, never queries the GPU (nvidia-smi is a
# stub), writes no NOTES.md / alert / ntfy. MOCK_* variables steer the stubs; MOCK_ORDER_FORM (mock only) overrides the
# order.
set -u -o pipefail
exec 8>&- 9>&-     # no inherited lock descriptor reaches a child (this script holds none itself)
WS=/home/USER/ai-speed-testing/strata-compare
case ${1:-} in ""|--dry-run|--mock) ;; *) echo "usage: gap-afetch.sh [--dry-run | --mock] (got '${1:-}'): nothing run"; exit 2;; esac   # (review 11-09 #1)
AG=$WS/work/r23/afetch-gap
DRY=0; [ "${1:-}" = --dry-run ] && DRY=1
MOCK=0; [ "${1:-}" = --mock ] && MOCK=1
M=$AG/scratch/mock
[ $MOCK = 1 ] && { [ -x $M/lib/with_server.sh ] || { echo "--mock needs work/r23/afetch-gap/gap-mock-test.sh's stubs"; exit 2; }; }
# ---- one instance at a time (review 11-09 #2): before anything touches the output folder; the pid file is not inside it
PIDF=$WS/tmp/afetch-gap.driver.pid; [ $MOCK = 1 ] && PIDF=$M/driver.pid
alive_driver() { [ -n "$1" ] && kill -0 "$1" 2> /dev/null && tr '\0' ' ' < /proc/$1/cmdline 2> /dev/null | grep -q 'gap-afetch'; }
if [ $DRY = 0 ]; then
  for try in 1 2; do
    ( set -o noclobber; echo $$ > $PIDF ) 2> /dev/null && break
    op=$(cat $PIDF 2> /dev/null)
    if alive_driver "$op"; then echo "another gap-afetch.sh (pid $op) is running: not started, nothing touched"; exit 9; fi
    [ $try = 1 ] && rm -f $PIDF || { echo "the pid file $PIDF could not be taken: not started, nothing touched"; exit 9; }
  done
  [ "$(cat $PIDF 2> /dev/null)" = "$$" ] || { echo "the pid file $PIDF is not this driver's: not started, nothing touched"; exit 9; }
  trap '[ "$(cat $PIDF 2> /dev/null)" = "$$" ] && rm -f $PIDF' EXIT
fi
export RB_CACHE=$WS/tmp/r23                       # (before env.sh: its tool caches and TMPDIR go there)
[ $DRY = 1 ] && export RB_CACHE=$AG/scratch/rb-cache
[ $MOCK = 1 ] && export RB_CACHE=$M/rb-cache
source $WS/bringup/lib/env.sh
unset GUARD_MEM_GIB GUARD_VRAM_MIB GUARD_SWAP_GROW_GIB GUARD_VRAM_MODE GUARD_FOLLOW_PORT LR_MAX SPEED_FILE PROF_SAMPLING EXE ENVX NSYS COLD
for v in $(compgen -e | grep '^STRATA_'); do [ "$v" = STRATA_MON_GPU ] || unset "$v"; done   # no stray switch reaches an engine
for v in $(compgen -e | grep '^SQ_'); do unset "$v"; done                                    # nor a stray sampled-client setting
export PROMPT_DIR=$WS/bringup/out/r20a/prompts EVICT_GLOB="$WS/models/ISTA-GSQ-RCO/IQ3_S/*.gguf"
P=$WS/.venv/bin/python; PY="$P -I -B"; AFR=$AG/afetch_rules.py
FR=$WS/work/r23/basalt_fix_rules.py; KR=$WS/work/r22; LIB=$WS/bringup/lib; B90=$KR/basalt-pr90; Q=$WS/work/r23/sampled-qwen
BPD=/home/USER/ai-speed-testing/basalt-pr90-data
O=$WS/results/r23/adaptfetch/gap
[ $DRY = 1 ] && O=$AG/scratch/gap-dry
W28=$WS/strata-r22p028x; E28=$WS/engine-r22p028x; EAF=$WS/engine-r23afetch
Y16=$WS/results/r22/gap16/pfy/x28h; E7REF=x28h-e7a; PROF=$WS/bringup/out/logs/prof; COLDM=$WS/results/r22/gap17/bp90/cold-M.jsonl
LOCKPID=$WS/tmp/port-gap.lockpid; HOLD=/home/USER/ai/deep-research/tmp/bench2.hold
NOTE=$WS/configs/usability/bin/ntfy-note.py
STATE=$WS/work/qwen4-kit/hfwatch/state.json; SHAPE_RES=$WS/results/r23/port-0213/shape-gap/result.txt; SHAPE_UNIT=shape-gap0213
PRIO_DONE=$WS/tmp/afetch-priority-done
SPEC=$Q/spec-adaptfetch.json; SRVSH=$LIB/srv.sh; STOPMON=$WS/scripts/stopmon.sh
P028X_SHA=f4c4f654fb24; AF_SHA=153ce47d3ef0
MAXM=${AF_MAX_MIN:-150}
E7_MIN=5; PFY_MIN=10; B2_MIN=3; B3_MIN=5; VF_MIN=7; SQ8_MIN=5; SQ4_MIN=3; IDS_MIN=1; SCORE_MIN=18; DEC_MIN=1
SQ_REST=$(( 3 * SQ8_MIN + SQ4_MIN + IDS_MIN + SCORE_MIN + DEC_MIN ))   # 38: the sampled part after VF (all or nothing)
WORST_OVER=25                                                       # the worst case past the deadline (see the header)
NVSMI_T=20; GPUCLEAR_N=12; GPUCLEAR_S=5; GW_S=5; KGRACE_N=10; KGRACE_S=2; KTERM_S=10
